WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.350
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.770
Hello? Sota?

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.770
Listen, Big Sis...

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.490
Yes... I see...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.320
Here in Sakuragi Park,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.440
the Pokémon caught by Satoshi and Go
are enjoying another relaxed day.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.940
Huh? Where’s Messon, by the way?

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.990
I’m sure it’s somewhere in here...

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.410
But finding it’s gonna be tough.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.030
Wanpachi, I’m home!

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.490
Now there’s even more...

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.730
And I’m not done!

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.880
There’s still so many more
Pokémon out there in the world!

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.310
Oh.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.510
Listen, Go...

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.210
Sota just called me.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.390
It seems his friend has a problem.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.120
Could you come with me?

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.400
Sota?

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.150
He said his friend
brought her favorite Pokémon,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.990
and now the kids
got into a fight over it.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.110
A fight?

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:42.040
Something about whether
the Pokémon’s cute or not...

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.040
What’s that all about?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.620
I’m not sure.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.050
That’s why I figured
I’d ask you two for help.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:49.670
Of course!

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.170
If you want help
with Pokémon, then...

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.800
We’ve got you covered!

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.900
It really is a funny Pokémon!

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.620
That’s not true!

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.400
Hi-chan is cute!

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.510
Huh? No, it’s not cute at all!

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.600
Yeah!

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.710
Yes, it<i> is </i>cute!

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.700
Sota.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.760
Big Sis!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.820
Go, Satoshi, you’re here too?

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.140
Is that the friend you
mentioned on the phone?

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.910
Yeah. Her name’s Nami...

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.150
That’s a...

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.870
...Hinbass!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:27.620
PocketMonsters

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.040
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.630
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.340
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.220
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.550
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.220
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.730
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:52.980
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.570
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.490
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:07.250
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:14.250
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.460
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.800
Let's have a fight!

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.510
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.350
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.680
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:35.360
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.700
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.200
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.330
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.120
I choose you!

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:58.130
Hinbass's Pretty Scale

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.760
Hinbass! Fish Pokémon!
Water type!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.470
It is the shabbiest
Pokémon of all!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:11.300
It forms schools and lives at
the bottom of plant-filled rivers!

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.770
I see.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.670
Hey, Sota, you think this Pokémon
is weird too, don’t you?

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.780
Sota...

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.400
I, uh...

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.440
Huh? I think Hinbass is great.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.290
Not to mention, it evolves
into an amazing Pokémon!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.890
Huh? You’re lying!

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.420
There’s no way.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.790
No, I’m serious!

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:38.570
A Pikachu!
It really...

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.300
So cute!
It really...

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.160
So cute!

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.320
Yeah!

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.810
Pet, pet...

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.910
Poke, poke...

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.990
Nami...

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.130
It’s a real shame they can’t see
how great Hinbass is.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.280
Wanna come to
Sakuragi Park with us?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.780
There’s loads of Pokémon there.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:11.860
Yeah!

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.680
Hi-chan looks happy.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.210
Its name is Hi-chan?

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.530
Hi-chan the Hinbass.
Cute, huh?

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.190
Hi-chan...

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.390
Don’t worry.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.700
Looks like they’re friends already.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.410
See?
Nothing to worry about.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:48.070
Hi-chan made friends!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.310
You really care for it, huh?

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.080
Yup!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.200
Daddy gave it to me!
It’s so cute!

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.960
But everyone says it isn’t...

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:04.480
You said Hi-chan evolves into
an amazing Pokémon... Was that true?

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.210
Yeah!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:11.970
That’s right.
Hinbass evolves into Milokaross.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.720
Isn’t that amazing, Nami?
It’ll take everyone by surprise!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.590
Yeah!

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:18.100
But you know,

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.750
raising Hinbass to Milokaross
is hardly a walk in the park.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.360
It won’t be evolving any time soon.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.230
Aw, really?

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.860
Yeah, it’s real tough!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.110
It might take a while,

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.900
but I’m sure it’ll evolve!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:36.270
That's right! Just try to bond with Hinbass
and raise it with care.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.250
It will evolve someday!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.410
Yeah, I’ll treat it with care!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:45.380
But as it is now, nobody in kindergarten
will see how great Hi-chan is.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.910
Hinbass is cool, though!

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:49.630
Okay, we heard you
the first time.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.650
Oh, I know! You could try this!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.810
Right...

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:03.270
“Water Festival We’re All Friends
Water-type Pokémon Friendship Contest”.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.400
It’s a contest for Water-type Pokémon only,
held in Kaina City in the Hoenn Region.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.540
A Water-type Pokémon contest?!

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.160
I wanna participate!

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:17.160
I’m afraid the contest is for
kids younger than you.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.370
Oh...

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.180
Maybe you could join this contest.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.490
Oh, yes! If you win there,

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.780
everyone might see
how great your Hinbass is!

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.630
Really?

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.750
But winning won’t be easy...

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.860
I’ll do it!

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:32.620
All right!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.830
We’ll cheer you on
so you can win!

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.400
I’ll support you
as good as I can!

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.780
First we’d better research the contest
and make a plan!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.010
Geez...
First we’d better research the contest
and make a plan!

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.140
First we’d better research the contest
and make a plan!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.150
If you don’t try,
you’ll never succeed.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.960
Hi-chan!

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.080
Let’s enter the contest, together!

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.830
So, what do they do in this contest?

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.660
Huh?

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.820
It says “Swim with your Pokémon,
showcase your moves,

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.200
“and show off the appeal of
your close friendship.”

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.050
Now, Nami!

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.550
Let’s get right to
practicing with Hi-chan!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.470
Training! Training!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.140
Yeah!

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.350
All right, Hi-chan!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.230
Use Tackle!

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.820
Good! One more time!

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.980
Hey, Satoshi!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.430
The contest is <i>not</i> about battling!

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.240
Huh?!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.380
Sorry...

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:39.240
Battling really is
the <i>only</i> thing on your mind.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.450
Well, then, what would <i>you</i> do?

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:46.390
Let’s see... Since I’d be performing
in an aquarium, I’d start by...

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.790
...sharing a friendly swim
with my Pokémon, maybe?

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.300
Huh? That’s so boring.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:53.050
Nami?

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.490
I... can’t swim.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.810
<i>What?!</i>

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:03.310
Then I’m not sure if you
can even enter the contest...

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.170
But I want to win!

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:10.360
I want everyone to understand
that Hi-chan is wonderful and cute!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.390
I’ll help you, Nami.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:32.710
Let’s give it our all, together!

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.630
Thank you, Big Sis!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.340
And...

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.840
You, too, Hi-chan!

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.970
Which leaves...

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.580
Satoshi! Go! Give us a hand!

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.500
That should do it, yeah?

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.640
So, what’s the plan, Koharu?

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.000
First we’ll have Nami
practice swimming here.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.780
You two help Hi-chan train.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.780
In order to win in a contest,
you need things like beauty and cuteness, too.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:05.410
Teach Hi-chan to swim
more elegantly.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.260
Elegantly...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.630
Oh, I know! Tosakinto!

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.090
Can you help us?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.050
And what about me?

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.560
You two help, too.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.660
Got it!

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.830
All right... Let’s start by
having you get used to the water.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:27.720
Okay.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.070
Almost had it!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.370
Yeah, that’s the spirit!

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.310
Now I’ll try... Hah!

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:44.200
Are you sure this’ll work?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:45.640
Absolutely.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.500
All right, Tosakinto... Go!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.570
Now you try, Hi-chan.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.730
Can they do this in time?

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:23.560
PocketMonsters

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.200
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.580
PocketMonsters

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:34.500
Water
Hinbass
PocketMonsters

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.790
All right! Great jump!

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:48.040
And you’ve gotten
better at swimming!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.600
How are you guys, Koharu?

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.230
Looking good.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.950
Look, Big Sis! I swam!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.640
Good job, Nami!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:01.990
Yes, that was perfect!

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.060
So I guess it’s almost time...

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:06.120
...to swim with Hi-chan!

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:08.950
Yup!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.270
Go on.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.880
Looks like Hi-chan
really loves Nami, too.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.240
Yup!

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.700
Okay, time to practice together.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.010
Yes!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.270
That’s it for today.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.530
Okay! Hi-chan, you did great!

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:41.530
Huh?

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.680
This scale’s got a different color.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.160
That’s right!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.660
You’re right!

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.740
Isn’t it pretty?

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.620
Yeah, it’s super pretty!

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.850
Right?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.590
Koharu.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.450
I thought you weren’t interested
in Pokémon at all?

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.530
O-Oh, quiet, you.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:05.090
Seeing Nami and Hi-chan work so hard
made me want to cheer them on.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.180
Wouldn’t it be great?

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:09.640
To see them win.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.410
Yeah.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:19.810
Kaina City, Hoenn Region

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:22.570
We’re here!
The day has come!
Kaina City, Hoenn Region

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:29.750
It’ll be fine!
Just do what we practiced!

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.550
Got it!
Let’s give it our all, Hi-chan!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.750
We’ll be rooting for you!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.510
Let’s see, the contest’s at—

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:36.200
There!
Let’s see, the contest’s at—

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:36.210
Let’s see, the contest’s at—

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.220
All right!

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:50.850
Camome’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.290
All right! I got Camome!

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.620
Hey, Go!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.980
I will never let a chance
at a catch get away!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.980
Every Pokémon is an important step
toward my dream!

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:03.530
Dream?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:04.780
Yeah!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:09.620
So Nami, you work hard on realizing your dream
of making everyone respect Hi-chan, too!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.120
Sure!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:17.000
We follow the brat boys to try and catch Pikachu,
and what do we find?

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.750
I didn’t know they were
holding a contest!

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:22.690
It’s a veritable buffet table of Pokémon!

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:25.760
We’ll nab loads of Pokémon
along with Pikachu, meow!

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:35.640
That was Rito and Sunnygo, everyone!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.730
Impressive!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.950
They were in pretty good sync.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:42.530
Next up are Marin and Azumao!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.250
Yeah!

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:49.240
Winning this might be tough.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.120
That’s not true!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.760
Nami and Hi-chan are
in perfect sync, too!

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:54.780
Yeah!

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.560
They practiced like crazy!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.960
Oh, come to think of it, wasn’t this contest
getting streamed online, too?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:07.210
That’s right. So I asked Mom...

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:11.470
...to invite their friends from the kindergarten
to watch it at our house.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:20.590
Next up are Nami and
Hi-chan the Hinbass!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.700
Go ahead!

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.560
Hinbass? Like, for reals?

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:31.480
That’s, like, <i>so</i> ugly!

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.160
Stop, Big Sis!

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.580
Here we go, Hi-chan!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:49.800
All right!
They’re off to a good start!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.840
The training with Koiking
paid off!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.350
I wanna try that, too!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.350
Looks fun!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.610
Whoa, it’s, like, actually good!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.740
They just might make it!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.490
That’s awesome, Nami!

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.840
Hi-chan, time for the finish!

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:16.950
Ready, and...

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:20.700
What’s this?!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:25.080
If you say “Uwah! What’s this?!”
or “What’s that?!”...

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.390
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:32.010
To protect the world from devastation.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.380
To preserve world peace.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:38.430
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.810
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.430
Musashi!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.690
Kojiro!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:47.150
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:50.490
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.740
Just kidding, meow!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.030
Team Rocket!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.040
Those two again?!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.540
Nami!

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.400
We’ll be taking
every Pokémon here!

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.170
That includes Pikachu,
of course!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.870
Not happening!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.050
We’ll take you on!

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:15.920
Pochama!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.970
Namakobushi!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.290
Starmie!

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.680
Give them back!

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:25.690
We’ll take that
feeble-looking one, too.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:26.940
No!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.430
Vending, come on!

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:38.750
Rocket...

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:39.280
Vending...

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.060
Secret!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.080
It’s electrifying!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.460
The Savage Pokémon,
Kibanha!

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:54.010
The Pincer Pokémon,
Kingler!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.430
Nami!

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.180
Big Sis!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.050
Kibanha! Bite!

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.220
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.450
Kingler! Metal Claw!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:13.900
Rabbifoot, dodge!

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.280
Hand it over, meow.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:29.500
Hi-chan!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.810
Your scale came off...

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.240
Hi-chan, are you okay?!

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.890
Stick back on! Stick back on!

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:56.310
Hi-chan...

00:18:56.310 --> 00:19:00.330
You struggle for nothing, meow!
I will be taking this one, meow!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.280
Don’t!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:02.550
What are you doing, meow?!

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.910
Move it, meow!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.040
What?!

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:19.170
What?!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.840
It evolved...

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:41.950
So beautiful...

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:48.560
Milokaross! Tender Pokémon!
Water type!

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:52.370
Said to be the most beautiful
Pokémon in the world!

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.260
Hi-chan?

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.090
I’m so glad, Hi-chan!

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.700
What’s that? I <i>so</i> want it!

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.100
Kibanha! Take Down!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.110
It’s Wrap!

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.170
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:40.580
Nami!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.760
Hi-chan, I believe in you!

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.180
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.690
Amazing!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:01.400
Hi-chan!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.750
We may have gone through
both this and that...

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:10.740
But Nami and Hi-chan showed us a marvelous
performance, a strong bond, and even an evolution,

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.310
earning them this special award!

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:15.090
I can’t believe it actually evolved!

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.960
It just started shining brightly,
and then...

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.570
I saw it! It was amazing!

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:21.150
So pretty!

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.020
I want a Hinbass, too!

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.840
Sorry I said it was
a weird Pokémon!

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:28.880
What a relief.

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:29.970
Yeah.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.710
Pokémon sure are amazing...

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:40.660
Our bonds with Pokémon
can bring forth unexpected miracles.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.400
It seems like Koharu’s heart
was moved, too.

